There is no obvious problem with what you have shown.

The programme has returned "warnings" which are not errors. These
warnings simply state that the shape of your perpendicular distance
histogram suggests the detection function rises at some distances, but
the distance sampling software prevents detection functions from
rising.  This does not interfere with the results of your analysis.

The first page of output you show is simply a 'glossary' defining the
terms used to label portions of the output.

