> > Reading the logs I see you have binned your distances (you have interval data) and there are 5 bins.  To these data you are fitting each of the key functions and using polynomial, cosine and Hermite adjustments respectively for HN, UNIF and HZ keys.  Note you are getting warnings about number of adjustments given the number of distance bins: 3 bins for normal+poly, 4 bins for UNIF+cos, and ***2 bins*** for HZ+Hermite.
> >
> > I would think that having only 2 bins with the HZ(2param)+Herm(another parameter) is where your bootstrap is going badly.  By chance in one or more bootstrap replicates you are getting all detections in the inner bin and none in the distant bin; Distance (inelegantly) falls over.
> >
> > I would either pull the adjustment terms off the HZ (and perhaps HN) or remove the HZ model from your bootstrapping altogether.
